  "reason": "Evidence: Multi-profile + avgpool + weighted fusion is clearly the best architecture (config_050: 0.6352, config_051: 0.6390). Within this setting, pca_n2000 substantially outperforms scgpt (0.6352 vs 0.5420 in config_009), but scvi_n200 has not yet been tested in the multi-profile regime. Uncertainty: We do not know where a learned deep generative encoder (scvi_n200, 200-dim latent) falls relative to linear PCA (pca_n2000, 2000-dim) — this is a major representation design choice that affects a large portion of the configuration space. Question tested: config_027 (scvi_n200, vit_l, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) is a single-variable swap from config_050 (pca_n2000, vit_l, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile), cleanly isolating the RNA encoder effect in the best-performing architecture. Why best next experiment: Resolving the RNA encoder ranking (pca vs scvi vs scgpt) in the top configuration is the highest-information experiment remaining — it either confirms PCA as sufficient (letting us focus budget on other axes) or reveals a better representation that could shift the entire search direction. It changes only one variable, making the result interpretable."
}

